course: dictionary
lesson: 11324
title: Yip, yap and yippee
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A yip is a short, high-pitched bark or cry, like the sound a small dog or a puppy makes. A coyote can make a yip too. «Coyotes howl, yip and bark to keep in touch with family» tells you the yips are part of how they talk to each other.
explain: Yip can also be a verb, so it can be an action. To yip means to make that sound. Look at the ending: yips, yipped and yipping show the word changing with time, like barked, barking and barks.
explain: Yip is not only an animal sound. People shout «yip!» or «yippee!» when they are excited and happy. Read the clues around the word to decide which meaning fits: is someone making a sound, or shouting for joy?
fact: A yip is a short, high-pitched bark or cry.
fact: To yip means to make a yip, like a puppy or a coyote.
fact: «Yip!» or «yippee!» is a shout of joy.
fact: «Yip and yap» describes a small dog that barks in a high, noisy way.
fact: Coyotes use yips and howls to call to their families at night.
exercise: «Coyotes howl, yip and bark to keep in touch with family.» What does yip mean? | A long, low growl | A bright, shining light | A big meal | *A short, high-pitched bark or cry
exercise: «Puppies yip when they want attention.» In this sentence, what kind of word is yip? | A noun, a thing | *A verb, an action word | A question word | An adjective, a describing word
exercise: People may shout «yip!» with excitement. What does the shout show? | Anger | Tiredness | Hunger | *Joy
test: «Real coyotes use no rockets or traps: they stalk, chase and pounce, and call to their families with yips and howls at night.» What do coyotes use to call to their families? | Bells | Rockets | Traps | *Yips and howls
test: In the phrase «a happy yip», what kind of word is yip? | A verb | *A noun | An interjection | A colour
exam: Why might a puppy yip? | To pay for its dinner | To sleep quietly all night | *To ask for attention | To fly across the room
